WEBVTT

00:52:28.333 --> 00:52:30.393
That is part of the experience of passion.

00:52:30.417 --> 00:52:32.476
It's a force that cannot be resisted.

00:52:32.500 --> 00:52:35.143
So why do we say "this is grandiose"

00:52:35.167 --> 00:52:38.018
versus "this is people
who have deep passion for something?"

00:52:38.042 --> 00:52:41.559
I agree with you, but I do think
that there is a bias in it too.

00:52:41.583 --> 00:52:42.851
AG: Yeah, there might be.

00:52:42.875 --> 00:52:45.809
I think it depends for me in part
on the valor and distinction

00:52:45.833 --> 00:52:49.518
between what's called harmonious
versus obsessive passion.

00:52:49.542 --> 00:52:51.309
So harmonious passion is, you know,

00:52:51.333 --> 00:52:54.768
I love it, I chose it,
I'm excited to pursue this work.

00:52:54.792 --> 00:52:57.976
And I think if that's
the experience of passion you have,

00:52:58.000 --> 00:53:00.518
often the work in and of itself
is its own reward.